    "MissionGiver": "Headhunters",
    "Title": "Tactical Strike",
    "TitleKey": "HeadHunters_ShipAmbush_VH_title_001",
    "Description": "Some folks don\u2019t seem happy with us. Got word that several sub-capital ships and a number of escorts are targeting our ops. Figured the best way to keep \u2018em from causing us trouble is to hit them before they hit us. \n\nWe got eyes on a <EM4>~mission(AmbushTarget)</EM4> that\u2019s part of this squad, and it looks like they regularly pass by <EM4>~mission(Location|Address)</EM4>, a spot tailor made for a surprise attack. A nearby emission cloud can hide you and anyone you bring along for muscle.\n\nNo sugarcoating it. This ain\u2019t gonna be easy. But the payoff should make it worth your while. Finish the job and the main contractor gets a bonus <EM4>~mission(ScripAmount) Council Scrip</EM4>. \n\nPlus, who knows what kinda good stuff you\u2019ll find floating in all that wreckage.\n\nStows out.",
    "DescriptionKey": "HeadHunters_ShipAmbush_VH_desc_001",
    "DisplayDescription": "Some folks don\u2019t seem happy with us. Got word that several sub-capital ships and a number of escorts are targeting our ops. Figured the best way to keep \u2018em from causing us trouble is to hit them before they hit us. \n\nWe got eyes on a <EM4>[AmbushTarget]</EM4> that\u2019s part of this squad, and it looks like they regularly pass by <EM4>Asteroid Mining Base</EM4>, a spot tailor made for a surprise attack. A nearby emission cloud can hide you and anyone you bring along for muscle.\n\nNo sugarcoating it. This ain\u2019t gonna be easy. But the payoff should make it worth your while. Finish the job and the main contractor gets a bonus <EM4>[ScripAmount] Council Scrip</EM4>. \n\nPlus, who knows what kinda good stuff you\u2019ll find floating in all that wreckage.\n\nStows out.",
